// vesta host <-> guest channel, protocol version 1.0 (ARCHITECTURE §2.3).
//
// Transport: AF_VSOCK in the guest. vesta-guestd listens on CTRL port 22085
// and EVT port 22086 (configurable, see docs/compat/kata-4.2.md §3). The host
// always initiates connections, one CTRL and one EVT connection per sandbox.
// Hybrid vsock (CLH/Dragonball/Firecracker): the host writes
// "CONNECT <port>\n" on the sandbox UDS and expects a line starting "OK ".
//
// Framing (both connections, both directions): each frame is a 4-byte
// unsigned big-endian length N followed by N bytes of one protobuf message.
// 1 <= N <= 1048576 (1 MiB). A receiver closes the connection on a length
// outside that range, on a message that fails to decode, or on a message
// type not valid for that connection and direction. It never allocates more
// than N bytes for a frame, and it reads a frame within a deadline.
//
// Frame types:
//   CTRL host -> guest: ControlRequest
//   CTRL guest -> host: ControlResponse
//   EVT  both ways:     EventStreamMessage (see events.proto for which
//                       variants each side may send)
//
